  "changes": [
    "A user-started foreground dictation stays active across provider end-of-speech and final phrase callbacks, in both hold and tap modes.",
    "Confirmed phrases are inserted once; later silence, cancellation or service failure cannot erase previously inserted text.",
    "The same recognition engine and strict local-mode policy are retained. Silence/no-match rearm within the active gesture; busy and immediately failing services have bounded backoff.",
    "Stop, release, screen pause, preview, closing and editor replacement invalidate pending restarts and stale callbacks.",
    "Provider silence hints request 10 seconds; the 90-second provider watchdog rotates a phrase instead of ending dictation.",
    "The voice panel and pointer target remain mounted; editor focus restores only after an explicit stop."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Recognition is provided by the selected Android speech service. Silence extras are provider hints and rearming can have a short service-dependent gap.",
    "Regression tests drive controlled recognition callbacks, Android adapters and real Compose gestures. Physical microphone accuracy and provider timing on the user phone were not measured."
  ],
